{"model": "Chatterbox Turbo (MLX 8-bit)", "segments": [{"text": "I have worked on several projects that need a reporting tool to present the data models in a complex manor.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/451c16840bf708f16906b436c4774466f32a9a07fbb4e5f9b222b1eee8a18add.mp3", "words": [[2, 0.34, 0.48], [3, 0.48, 0.64], [4, 0.64, 0.94], [5, 0.94, 1.44], [6, 1.44, 1.68], [7, 1.68, 1.82], [8, 1.82, 1.94], [9, 1.94, 2.3], [10, 2.3, 2.7], [11, 2.7, 2.92], [12, 2.92, 3.18], [13, 3.18, 3.42], [14, 3.42, 3.62], [15, 3.62, 3.98], [16, 3.98, 4.14], [17, 4.14, 4.24], [18, 4.24, 4.62]]}, {"text": "I often find these queries to get more complicated than ActiveRecord is able to handle (think needing sub-arqueries or joining against tables that aren’t represented by models).", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ca43ca5f55dbb62855bdd0966715953638dad34d8544efa4f08432d5a033b92e.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.46], [2, 0.46, 0.78], [3, 0.78, 1.02], [4, 1.02, 1.34], [5, 1.34, 1.58], [6, 1.58, 1.7], [7, 1.7, 1.88], [8, 1.88, 2.46], [9, 2.46, 2.68], [11, 3.3, 3.46], [12, 3.46, 3.66], [13, 3.66, 3.82], [14, 3.82, 4.24], [15, 4.66, 4.92], [16, 4.92, 5.22], [18, 6.04, 6.22], [19, 6.22, 6.48], [20, 6.48, 6.92], [21, 6.92, 7.24], [22, 7.24, 7.48], [23, 7.48, 7.74], [24, 7.74, 8.2], [25, 8.2, 8.4], [26, 8.4, 8.74]]}, {"text": "As a result, I have to write raw SQL queries to handle the data retrieval.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/478338155c627a6bb44d87f1c44ba27a04aa135e55f3989c787e0c19a74cf882.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.3], [2, 0.3, 0.58], [3, 0.78, 0.84], [4, 0.84, 0.96], [5, 0.96, 1.12], [6, 1.12, 1.24], [7, 1.24, 1.5], [8, 1.5, 1.9], [9, 1.9, 2.3], [10, 2.3, 2.58], [11, 2.58, 2.86], [12, 2.86, 3.06], [14, 3.36, 3.78]]}, {"text": "This can get ugly very quickly if you are not careful on how you structure your framework for storing these queries.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/e172eda976948b5ed1e506d59259df854b9e2d8d1d37ededd00735da9b67349b.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.18, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.52], [3, 0.52, 0.72], [4, 0.72, 1.0], [5, 1.0, 1.4], [6, 1.4, 1.76], [7, 1.76, 1.9], [8, 1.9, 1.98], [9, 1.98, 2.2], [10, 2.2, 2.66], [11, 2.66, 2.92], [12, 2.92, 3.06], [13, 3.06, 3.22], [14, 3.22, 3.56], [15, 3.56, 3.82], [16, 3.82, 4.18], [17, 4.18, 4.54], [18, 4.54, 4.88], [19, 4.88, 5.12], [20, 5.12, 5.46]]}, {"text": "I am going to describe the two ways that I have solved this issue and give you the pros and cons of each.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/7a21e71f8e31310f78d808d7951b156ce1695245e10679fcaa0ddde0fa54e598.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.5], [3, 0.5, 0.68], [4, 0.68, 1.02], [5, 1.02, 1.26], [6, 1.26, 1.5], [7, 1.5, 1.74], [8, 1.74, 1.98], [9, 1.98, 2.1], [10, 2.1, 2.2], [11, 2.2, 2.48], [12, 2.48, 2.76], [13, 2.76, 3.12], [14, 3.12, 3.62], [15, 3.62, 3.78], [16, 3.78, 3.92], [17, 3.92, 4.06], [18, 4.06, 4.34], [19, 4.34, 4.62], [20, 4.62, 4.92], [21, 4.92, 5.2], [22, 5.2, 5.44]]}, {"text": "This will be the first article of two describing what the first iteration of this framework and why I choose to redesign it to something else.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/4c7184edc273f45a48d69c45eb2ef2202aad83fc15e570f1a6e6686f923aa1f6.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.26, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.48], [3, 0.48, 0.6], [4, 0.6, 0.76], [5, 0.76, 1.14], [6, 1.14, 1.4], [7, 1.4, 1.62], [8, 1.62, 2.22], [9, 2.22, 2.48], [10, 2.48, 2.64], [11, 2.64, 2.94], [12, 2.94, 3.3], [13, 3.3, 3.62], [14, 3.62, 3.84], [15, 3.84, 4.18], [16, 4.18, 4.7], [17, 4.7, 4.92], [18, 4.92, 5.06], [19, 5.06, 5.22], [20, 5.22, 5.54], [21, 5.54, 5.9], [22, 5.9, 6.14], [23, 6.14, 6.24], [24, 6.24, 6.5], [25, 6.5, 6.78]]}, {"text": "reports.rb", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b7de80cbd7bd9c3891219c18326477076fd0f711a85d4264bb400c1efb0174e3.mp3"}, {"text": "The first strategy involved creating a model called ‘reports’.", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8c687698311865a9f34ab844aa339b979c8b72c3a5fd460265e14bb08e76f213.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.76], [3, 0.76, 1.12], [4, 1.12, 1.58], [5, 1.58, 1.78], [6, 1.78, 2.02], [7, 2.02, 2.38]]}, {"text": "This model only contained basic information of the report: (name, url_name, created_at, etc.)", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/e0d0f32e54fa890bc13b9d6ab37010a357014e341e05195400b38c01dbaaaad3.mp3"}, {"text": "For every report we wanted to have, we would create a new entry in the database with that information filled out.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/fd91e870148372db53e1a9490ef2d05b120417ec37de141b3599e9fd2bb97a44.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.5], [2, 0.5, 0.82], [3, 0.82, 1.02], [4, 1.02, 1.22], [5, 1.22, 1.4], [6, 1.4, 1.72], [7, 2.14, 2.22], [8, 2.22, 2.34], [9, 2.34, 2.62], [10, 2.62, 2.8], [11, 2.8, 2.98], [12, 2.98, 3.36], [13, 3.36, 3.56], [14, 3.56, 3.66], [15, 3.66, 4.02], [16, 4.02, 4.36], [17, 4.36, 4.54], [18, 4.54, 5.08], [19, 5.08, 5.38], [20, 5.38, 5.66]]}, {"text": "These reports need to be install via rake tasks or migrations (to be honest, my personal preference is to use migrations, because when setting up a new box, you wont have to remember to run this other task).", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/acbbe3cee60e782f2c13de1004a97e8ab449d97d8bf504e0a8c4a9434eb73170.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.58], [3, 0.84, 0.98], [4, 0.98, 1.08], [6, 1.36, 1.68], [7, 1.68, 1.92], [8, 1.92, 2.24], [9, 2.24, 2.72], [10, 2.72, 3.32], [11, 3.8, 3.86], [12, 3.86, 3.96], [13, 3.96, 4.22], [14, 4.46, 4.54], [15, 4.54, 4.98], [16, 4.98, 5.36], [17, 5.36, 5.7], [18, 5.7, 5.86], [19, 5.86, 6.1], [20, 6.1, 6.72], [21, 6.72, 7.38], [22, 7.38, 7.56], [23, 7.56, 7.84], [24, 7.84, 8.0], [25, 8.0, 8.12], [26, 8.12, 8.26], [27, 8.26, 8.52], [28, 8.88, 8.96], [30, 9.26, 9.34], [31, 9.34, 9.46], [32, 9.46, 9.72], [33, 9.72, 9.96], [34, 9.96, 10.12], [35, 10.12, 10.34], [36, 10.34, 10.58], [37, 10.58, 11.04]]}, {"text": "lib/reports.rb", "block": 6, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/46a656add48b9032d64b1f11a8c1df6628bbcbf6dca3d3c615ef5d3ef8c88c3d.mp3"}, {"text": "Now that we know what reports are available, the next step is create their methods.", "block": 7, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/20df94de578d30ea9974b08470a545cdcf9ce6cc5306baefab550ba6027bf512.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.48], [3, 0.48, 0.68], [4, 0.68, 0.92], [5, 0.92, 1.32], [6, 1.32, 1.52], [7, 1.52, 1.92], [8, 2.28, 2.36], [9, 2.36, 2.6], [10, 2.6, 2.84], [11, 2.84, 3.06], [12, 3.06, 3.3], [13, 3.3, 3.48], [14, 3.48, 3.78]]}, {"text": "Each report gets its own method in lib/reports.rb, because that is where we will be storing the SQL and formatting rules for each of them.", "block": 7, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8753677b481a35a9f3c5f23fa33849706a2cb8990fab729880b4b4aa33e3b172.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.58], [2, 0.58, 0.86], [3, 0.86, 1.02], [4, 1.02, 1.2], [5, 1.2, 1.54], [6, 1.54, 1.74], [8, 2.92, 3.5], [9, 3.5, 3.7], [10, 3.7, 3.82], [11, 3.82, 4.0], [12, 4.0, 4.18], [13, 4.18, 4.32], [14, 4.32, 4.46], [15, 4.46, 4.74], [16, 4.74, 4.92], [18, 5.24, 5.48], [19, 5.48, 5.78], [20, 5.78, 6.14], [21, 6.14, 6.42], [22, 6.42, 6.6], [23, 6.6, 6.72], [24, 6.72, 6.9]]}, {"text": "An example report would look something like this:", "block": 8, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8d49ba0ea404f5bdf0de7caab093ed8cc89f3f8c99120e4c7a83af4634d5508c.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.14], [1, 0.14, 0.5], [2, 0.5, 0.8], [3, 0.8, 1.04], [4, 1.04, 1.22], [5, 1.22, 1.5], [6, 1.5, 1.78], [7, 1.78, 2.06]]}, {"text": "Each method returns a [NxM] array of the results, ready to displayed in the html.", "block": 9, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/c6acd03de9cd3ce691aced3e26c32b8f52a4b96e9b8923f88f0c0bd5d74e2724.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.58], [2, 0.58, 0.98], [3, 0.98, 1.26], [4, 1.26, 2.14], [5, 2.14, 2.4], [6, 2.4, 2.56], [7, 2.56, 2.62], [8, 2.62, 2.96], [9, 3.46, 3.6], [10, 3.6, 3.76], [12, 4.08, 4.24], [13, 4.24, 4.34]]}, {"text": "Pagination and sorting have been withheld from this example, as they are trivial to add in.", "block": 9, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/156d0da52a27d90fc75c39f819e6424248e6c842dd5d238bc1eb15ab90026a9e.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.66, 0.92], [2, 0.92, 1.2], [3, 1.2, 1.5], [4, 1.5, 1.74], [5, 1.74, 2.14], [6, 2.14, 2.34], [7, 2.34, 2.56], [8, 2.56, 3.04], [9, 3.36, 3.56], [10, 3.56, 3.68], [11, 3.68, 3.76], [12, 3.76, 4.1], [13, 4.1, 4.34], [14, 4.34, 4.52], [15, 4.52, 4.72]]}, {"text": "Kaminari gem handles pagination very nicely, although for larger reports, I letting the database handle the pagination, ruby will have to loop through all of the data points, which is expensive.", "block": 9, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/85c20b7cf17e9af96cc2d1b28630674e0b9e921eee6f5afad6d15a2833817f41.mp3", "words": [[2, 0.8, 1.2], [3, 1.2, 1.78], [4, 1.78, 2.08], [5, 2.08, 2.52], [6, 3.02, 3.28], [7, 3.28, 3.48], [8, 3.48, 3.82], [9, 3.82, 4.26], [10, 4.64, 4.68], [11, 4.68, 4.98], [12, 4.98, 5.14], [13, 5.14, 5.42], [14, 5.42, 5.86], [15, 5.86, 6.0], [16, 6.0, 6.7], [17, 7.22, 7.36], [18, 7.36, 7.62], [19, 7.62, 7.76], [20, 7.76, 7.94], [21, 7.94, 8.14], [22, 8.14, 8.38], [23, 8.38, 8.6], [24, 8.6, 8.76], [25, 8.76, 8.84], [26, 8.84, 9.04], [27, 9.04, 9.34], [28, 9.34, 9.62], [29, 9.62, 9.76], [30, 9.76, 10.22]]}, {"text": "reports_controller.rb", "block": 10, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f6928c453b2c4c9357a6b54b05c0f031b7aa136d42a1db867de52f0237493ca4.mp3"}, {"text": "Next a reports controller needs to get made.", "block": 11, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/4fd37452467e19e151ba5b271b62e6816ab91be9b698d1b6818a3a43ae2aecf5.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.4], [2, 0.58, 1.06], [3, 1.06, 1.44], [4, 1.44, 1.7], [5, 1.7, 1.92], [6, 1.92, 2.06], [7, 2.06, 2.36]]}, {"text": "This will have two methods in it: index, and show.", "block": 11, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/0d6a9c6e676ddf4a05853816258a06e779f07729c8de3d6633f0979f232c9c4f.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.26], [2, 0.26, 0.38], [3, 0.38, 0.58], [4, 0.58, 0.84], [5, 0.84, 1.04], [6, 1.04, 1.2], [7, 1.66, 1.88], [8, 1.88, 2.34], [9, 2.34, 2.56]]}, {"text": "All index will do is show the list of report names and links to them (we used a drop down box with textboxes for begin and end date selectors).", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/c66ce55c296a23cf7a09c090483d9964e978ce62dc94cf40cf138f0a80ba6cb8.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.58], [2, 0.58, 0.84], [3, 0.84, 1.08], [4, 1.08, 1.32], [5, 1.32, 1.58], [6, 1.58, 1.78], [7, 1.78, 2.02], [8, 2.02, 2.14], [9, 2.14, 2.42], [10, 2.42, 2.8], [11, 2.8, 3.12], [12, 3.12, 3.3], [13, 3.3, 3.56], [14, 3.56, 3.84], [15, 4.2, 4.3], [19, 4.74, 4.96], [20, 4.96, 5.2], [21, 5.2, 5.42], [23, 6.0, 6.24], [24, 6.24, 6.52], [25, 6.52, 6.74], [26, 6.74, 6.98], [27, 6.98, 7.14], [28, 7.14, 7.78]]}, {"text": "Show is where the report will be displayed.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d8c0fd65072d03946e85cf3566629ddbd92993e2bed2cec99b659daaf2d3fa05.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.56], [2, 0.56, 0.74], [3, 0.74, 0.88], [4, 0.88, 1.18], [5, 1.18, 1.46], [6, 1.46, 1.6], [7, 1.6, 2.0]]}, {"text": "We probably should of made this an AJAX callback and requested the results separately, but I will get to that later.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/58ec9469af0db612405efa610f2a13cd5123f9f2c7b4a162e366529f608fb435.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.52], [2, 0.52, 0.84], [4, 1.18, 1.34], [5, 1.34, 1.52], [6, 1.52, 1.66], [7, 1.66, 2.08], [8, 2.08, 2.5], [9, 2.5, 2.7], [10, 2.7, 3.1], [11, 3.1, 3.26], [12, 3.26, 3.48], [13, 3.48, 3.98], [14, 4.24, 4.34], [15, 4.34, 4.42], [16, 4.42, 4.54], [17, 4.54, 4.66], [18, 4.66, 4.82], [19, 4.82, 4.92], [20, 4.92, 5.18]]}, {"text": "The show method would grab from the URL the url_name of the report being run.", "block": 13, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/1534e09883468ec7e56a40f19935a148e8caf71216c56beeab0fc76359600a9a.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.38], [2, 0.38, 0.7], [3, 0.7, 0.96], [4, 0.96, 1.24], [5, 1.24, 1.5], [6, 1.5, 1.68], [7, 1.68, 2.04], [8, 2.04, 2.42], [10, 3.9, 4.26], [11, 4.26, 4.38], [12, 4.38, 4.7], [13, 4.7, 5.02], [14, 5.02, 5.36]]}, {"text": "Then it would run .send to execute the method name of the string in the lib/reports.rb class.", "block": 13, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/bc831f6133d1384d5ef3af48d0d7793066fade6c10508d646fccca45a7eab5ab.mp3"}, {"text": "The results were written to a table element with a timestamp of when the report was run.", "block": 13, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/88fbca55edbc9cc435f37e1371dfa2bc468487c35fcfe12f871ac61011646e3f.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.44], [2, 0.44, 0.64], [3, 0.64, 0.86], [4, 0.86, 1.04], [5, 1.04, 1.14], [6, 1.14, 1.36], [7, 1.36, 1.74], [8, 1.74, 1.94], [9, 1.94, 2.08], [11, 2.64, 2.78], [12, 2.78, 2.9], [13, 2.9, 3.02], [14, 3.02, 3.24], [15, 3.24, 3.48], [16, 3.48, 3.7]]}, {"text": "Brakeman hates this, because using .to_sym on any parameter is a huge security flaw.", "block": 14, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/c4e8e2644a75aa0400a16819cd7abecabd6a79f010a3d9d392df22dd73ebffcd.mp3"}, {"text": "This reporting engine was locked behind CanCan/Devise and only staff members had access to this page.", "block": 14, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/05d68ffdfc7c56a5614cf76b018bcfbec2d99e441e539074b6c25001142947eb.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.62], [2, 0.62, 0.96], [3, 0.96, 1.2], [4, 1.2, 1.44], [5, 1.44, 1.8], [7, 2.86, 3.18], [8, 3.18, 3.42], [9, 3.42, 3.7], [10, 3.7, 4.04], [11, 4.04, 4.24], [12, 4.24, 4.58], [13, 4.58, 4.82], [14, 4.82, 4.98], [15, 4.98, 5.4]]}, {"text": "But someone malicious could of done a lot of damage to the system if abused.", "block": 14, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8cfdc87b5395e757eae2d62bb9476baa15f1781e30ed4f6b1dc298ca90141455.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.46], [2, 0.46, 0.88], [3, 0.88, 1.28], [5, 1.4, 1.54], [6, 1.54, 1.68], [7, 1.68, 1.86], [8, 1.86, 2.02], [9, 2.02, 2.28], [10, 2.28, 2.52], [11, 2.52, 2.64], [12, 2.64, 3.02], [13, 3.02, 3.26], [14, 3.26, 3.58]]}, {"text": "Pros", "block": 15, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b629726cd0b7234801e4206158e2f3f01af19022d4ec31a955fc5ec72c680845.mp3"}, {"text": "Custom sql == more control over the queries allowing for greater efficiency", "block": 16, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/2af01c1608c65268a3d26dac459d8fc4aab96d0f92ffcc40b8f5a4ded4a19c1f.mp3", "words": [[3, 0.76, 1.08], [4, 1.08, 1.5], [5, 1.5, 1.84], [6, 1.84, 2.0], [7, 2.0, 2.3], [8, 2.3, 2.72], [9, 2.72, 3.02], [10, 3.02, 3.3], [11, 3.3, 3.86]]}, {"text": "SQL is managed in GIT, so you can easily view the changes", "block": 17, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ff22e9bebc76cb2fd19d48c0aa04bb4b244b2bf3de8625124c189c4fbc85bf3e.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.46, 0.62], [2, 0.62, 0.9], [3, 0.9, 1.16], [4, 1.16, 1.66], [5, 1.66, 2.14], [6, 2.14, 2.26], [7, 2.26, 2.38], [8, 2.38, 2.72], [9, 2.72, 2.96], [10, 2.96, 3.12], [11, 3.12, 3.46]]}, {"text": "Formatting is handled by RoR, which lets you make use of the helper methods", "block": 18, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/43c436a352590928fb2da4908e034b834690c00256dd9ad303fa76ebeb617a86.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.56], [1, 0.56, 0.72], [2, 0.72, 0.98], [3, 0.98, 1.24], [5, 2.0, 2.22], [6, 2.22, 2.42], [7, 2.42, 2.58], [8, 2.58, 2.74], [9, 2.74, 3.0], [10, 3.0, 3.2], [11, 3.2, 3.32], [12, 3.32, 3.54], [13, 3.54, 3.88]]}, {"text": "Because the SQL lives in code, you can leverage ruby by creating custom ruby methods to generate portions of SQL.", "block": 19, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/c5c6a06266402cdbefc690d7547592638a0f8795f2164f1b5d03d3458e608704.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.48], [2, 0.48, 0.78], [3, 0.78, 1.02], [4, 1.02, 1.18], [5, 1.18, 1.46], [6, 1.74, 1.82], [7, 1.82, 1.94], [8, 1.94, 2.22], [9, 2.22, 2.52], [10, 2.52, 2.82], [11, 2.82, 3.16], [12, 3.16, 3.6], [13, 3.6, 3.88], [14, 3.88, 4.28], [15, 4.28, 4.58], [16, 4.58, 4.92], [17, 4.92, 5.38], [18, 5.38, 5.7], [19, 5.7, 6.02]]}, {"text": "(think a method the lets all reports sharing the same where conditions for datetime restrictions)", "block": 19, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/dbcfecd3942a4c7549bd84e5c1819f069566f827d27f2489d2e691576ae60f69.mp3"}, {"text": "Cons", "block": 20, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/888f900af800cdcbd6e947bed17fded4d9661d7ebf0cfc0bf47316d9b8bec67b.mp3"}, {"text": "You will end up with a massive lib/reports.rb file, which can be difficult to maintain", "block": 21, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/c27589a163b750fefb42a74f6c09a5cf695bbfc537fd399a40dd0b8d6bb19faa.mp3"}, {"text": "Because the formatting is handled by ruby, the report may run a little slow", "block": 22, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/514cb3ce1d063fb9a10c273c671ea9e057b9a2a29586de10e53e450d4bc2073d.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.48], [2, 0.48, 0.8], [3, 0.8, 1.14], [4, 1.14, 1.44], [5, 1.44, 1.72], [6, 1.72, 2.02], [7, 2.34, 2.4], [8, 2.4, 2.7], [9, 2.7, 2.98], [10, 2.98, 3.18], [11, 3.18, 3.34], [12, 3.34, 3.52], [13, 3.52, 3.86]]}, {"text": "Security flaw with the .send", "block": 23, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f852a74f6eb9a7a828d4f5bbc667bb2cd1aaeda3d236bc5bf6bf5542bec957b9.mp3"}, {"text": "Difficult to maintain.", "block": 24, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d6e6671b06ce28ca0b0d56ab512458ffc169a9136a173e90f4539416e7572ebe.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.44], [1, 0.44, 0.58], [2, 0.58, 0.82]]}, {"text": "If you change a column, then you have to modify your code a bunch of different places.", "block": 24, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/177d83c08214d043fb2816a756b077691cb00df03ac45e04080f21e33653b007.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.26, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.66], [4, 0.8, 1.08], [5, 1.64, 1.78], [6, 1.78, 1.96], [7, 1.96, 2.14], [8, 2.14, 2.3], [9, 2.3, 2.64], [10, 2.64, 2.84], [11, 2.84, 3.06], [12, 3.06, 3.18], [13, 3.18, 3.36], [14, 3.36, 3.5], [15, 3.5, 3.74], [16, 3.74, 4.14]]}, {"text": "Database dependency means for new deployments, a rake task, database migration, or seed must be run in order for the website to reflect the new reports", "block": 25, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/35ffd1cbde555fbc322887ef7535e985067c54e8ffbce61f534bf64c33c1a53f.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.46], [1, 0.46, 0.88], [2, 0.88, 1.52], [3, 1.52, 1.94], [4, 1.94, 2.1], [5, 2.1, 2.68], [6, 2.8, 2.82], [7, 2.82, 2.98], [8, 2.98, 3.3], [9, 3.7, 3.94], [10, 3.94, 4.66], [11, 5.06, 5.36], [13, 5.64, 5.88], [14, 5.88, 6.06], [15, 6.06, 6.26], [16, 6.26, 6.52], [17, 6.52, 6.72], [18, 6.72, 6.88], [19, 6.88, 6.98], [20, 6.98, 7.34], [21, 7.34, 7.56], [22, 7.56, 7.88], [23, 7.88, 8.12], [24, 8.12, 8.24], [25, 8.24, 8.56]]}, {"text": "Part 2 will be linked here.", "block": 26, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/69393f458090a8a11cd8e0f6450a0e546989795748e11eabcbff09729556cc98.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.26, 0.72], [2, 0.72, 1.04], [3, 1.04, 1.2], [4, 1.2, 1.52], [5, 1.52, 1.82]]}]}